course: dictionary
lesson: 12523
title: What does designation mean?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A designation is a name, title or label given to something or someone. It tells you what a thing is called or what job a person has. «Her job designation on the form is "lighthouse keeper".» The word shows her official title.
explain: Designation can also mean choosing or naming something for a special purpose. «The council announced the designation of the old wood as a protected area.» Here the council picked the wood and gave it a special name and status.
explain: This is a formal word, so you will often find it in official documents and serious writing. Look at the clues around it: words like official, job or protected tell you it means a formal name or label. To check, swap in the word "name" or "label". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A designation is a formal name, title or label.
fact: Useful phrases include «official designation» and «job designation».
fact: In science, a star may have a letter-and-number designation, which is a code that names it.
fact: «Designation» can also mean choosing or naming something for a special purpose, such as a protected area.
fact: A good check is to swap in "name" or "label" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Her job designation on the form is "teacher".» What does designation mean here? | *A job title or label | A sunny holiday abroad | A loud noise in the hall | A kind of wooden desk
exercise: «The council announced the designation of the wood as a protected area.» What does designation mean here? | *Choosing and naming it for a special purpose | Losing the map of the forest | Cutting down all the trees | A type of cold weather
exercise: Which phrase in these lessons means a formal name or label? | *official designation | kick the ball | jump high | blue sky
test: «The star has a letter-and-number designation, like AB7.» What does designation mean here? | Something you can eat | A long journey into space | *A name or code label | A bright light in the sky
test: Which sentence uses designation correctly? | The cake had a designation of chocolate. | *The dog's designation on the list is "Rex". | I designation the rain loudly. | The bus was designation fast.
exam: In «The official designation of the park is Greenfield Reserve», which word could replace designation without changing the meaning? | *name | wave | hole | noise
